{"key":"apphycem-mcq-025","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"B","final_answer":"local field but zero net flux contribution","working":"According to Gauss's Law, the total electric flux through a closed surface is proportional only to the net charge enclosed within that surface: $\\oint \\vec{E} \\cdot d\\vec{A} = Q_{\\text{encl}}/\\varepsilon_0$. The total electric field $\\vec{E}$ at any local point on the surface is the vector sum of fields from all charges, whether inside or outside. However, field lines from external charges that enter the volume must also exit, resulting in a net flux contribution of zero over the entire closed surface. Thus, external charges contribute to the local electric field on the surface, but contribute zero net flux.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":354,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":354,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":441,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":179,"reasoningTokens":262},"totalTokens":795,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":262,"promptTokenCount":354,"candidatesTokenCount":179,"totalTokenCount":795,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":354}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":179}]},"reasoningTokens":262,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3504,"keyed_label":"B"}
