{"key":"apphycem-mcq-028","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"B","final_answer":"lower potential and lower U","working":"The electrostatic force on a charge q is given by F = qE = -q grad(V). For a positive charge (q > 0), the force points in the direction of decreasing electric potential V. Since the charge is released from rest and subject only to this conservative electric force, it accelerates in the direction of the force, moving toward regions of lower electric potential. The electric potential energy is U = qV. Because q > 0, moving to a lower potential V corresponds directly to moving to a lower potential energy U (as potential energy is converted into kinetic energy). Therefore, it tends toward lower potential and lower U.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":363,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":363,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":452,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":168,"reasoningTokens":284},"totalTokens":815,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":284,"promptTokenCount":363,"candidatesTokenCount":168,"totalTokenCount":815,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":363}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":168}]},"reasoningTokens":284,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4533,"keyed_label":"B"}
